    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15768" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">endrŏmis</span></b> ,
		ĭdis, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνδρομίς</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a coarse woollen cloak in which the heated athletae
				wrapped themselves after their exercises</i>, <i><span class="en">Mart. 4,
			19</span></i>; <i><span class="en">14, 126</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Juv.
				3, 102</span></i>. But afterwards <i>a fine sort worn
				as an article of luxury</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tyriae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 6,
					246</span></i>
			 Rup.</div>
